versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.4.stable.mono.official [4c311cbee], v4.4.beta1.mono.official [d33da79d3], v4.4.beta1.official [d33da79d3]\n- Not reproducible in v4.3.stable.mono.official [77dcf97d8], v4.4.dev7.mono.official [46c8f8c5c], v4.4.dev7.official [46c8f8c5c]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 6750 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.11027.2001) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\n\nFor Button text that spans multiple lines, leading spaces are respected on the first line but not on following lines.  This was not the case in 4.3, where leading spaces on all lines are respected.  This affects all three alignment settings.  Appears to have been introduced between 4.4-dev7 and 4.4-beta1.\n\n4.3 behavior (left):\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eb24671d-6ffe-43d1-b80b-53d96ec2177d)\n\n4.4 behavior (left):\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/28e5de45-4bc9-4b24-a9d6-0d609e139c00)\n\n4.3 behavior (center):\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c5312965-99fa-44b1-98c7-6ea8c197b58c)\n\n4.4 behavior (center):\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2ab82db4-e4ce-4320-a9a0-d65266c2e324)\n\n4.3 behavior (right):\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fb64d37f-5f98-4044-8978-d3582a23d8b4)\n\n4.4 behavior (right):\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cc4d3ba3-a0d4-42f8-b737-dc2c84890d9e)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a Button node with default settings and enter text with five leading spaces, then press enter and enter a second line with five leading spaces.  The leading spaces on the second line will not display on the button.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[buttontextalign.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19209589/buttontextalign.zip)\n\nSee control.tscn.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo"